{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968153-new-fan-game-primal-the-ancient","id":968153,"title":"New Fan Game \"Primal, The Ancient\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T14:44:22-07:00","id":968153,"title":"New Fan Game \"Primal, The Ancient\"","content":"So, like the title says, I'm working on a new fan game for Chronicles of darkness. We'll start with what I've written so far, then go into more detail. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N-6WZ6J00kVNp9GnW8Rd1wnuGHS7x-QUph_4WGx-nK8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here it is</a> Now on to the more complicated bits,<br /> You play a warden, which in many ways resembles a sin eater. Like Sin-eaters, they formed an agreement with an ancient and powerful entity to save themselves from death; however, they never died, they merely came close. The creature they have bonded with is called a Primal, or a titan. It is a creature of elemental power which towers over the cities of mankind, or would, if it was allowed to walk the mortal world. In ancient days the Primal were bound by the gods (no one knows <i>which</i> gods) to only enter the world through the Pacts they form with wardens. When they break the rules of the pact, the nature of the pact punishes them (this is their integrity substitute).<br /> The Wardens have two types of powers (and I'm still working out the names for them) the first involves summoning just a piece of the Primal' true form, such as attacking your foes with a great talon of stone or wind, or using the strength of the titan to launch them into great leaps. These are powerful, but limited in scope. The only protection or improvement they can offer is to the warden himself, with everything else, they can only harm or kill. if one wants to bring health or aid, or build something one must use the second type of power (I am thinking of basing the names of Greek words, so the first set of powers would be named based on Soma {body}, and the second set would be based on Onoma {Name}) these powers use the conceptual connections to the elements (emotions, ideas, stories) to channel elemental energy into more utilitarian abilities (water based healing, controlling electricity, creating walls, and so on). These secondary powers are only accessible to wardens, due to the human perspective they bring to the primals. Their mana-equivalent is called dynam, and it comes in four types. Any type of dynam can be used to fuel any power, but it costs extra to fuel a power with the wrong dynam.<br /> The inborn splats of Wardens are the primary elemental affinity of their bonded primal, and the social splats are based on which of the laws of the pact the warden feels the strongest affinity with. I've got a law about punishing those who bring harm to humanity, and one about protecting the natural world. All the laws have more extreme elements, but some factions form around laws that aren't in the pact, as far as anyone can tell, which have a bad reputation. That and the document are all I've got for now, I'd love to here thoughts, ideas, rule tips, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew thought process.<br /> &quot;I have this great idea for a power/splat/merit/etc/&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no idea if this is balanced, useless, or gamebreaking.&quot;<br /> &quot;I'll ask the internet&quot;<br /> &quot;The thread has died.&quot; <img src=\"images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4226-spiderlord","name":"Spiderlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:59:11-07:00","id":968159,"title":"","content":"This really just reads like reskinned Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:06:53-07:00","id":968164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968153-new-fan-game-primal-the-ancient?p=968159#post968159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This really just reads like reskinned Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but agree. Saying &quot;they're like Sin-Eaters, but for primordial forces of the world&quot; is basically Werewolf, while the &quot;punishing mortals&quot; thing is core to Beast's MO. What do Primals do that nobody else does?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:20:04-07:00","id":968632,"title":"","content":"A Beast's atavisms change their own body, the simple powers of Primals extend through the environment, and the punishing thing is one social group. The Primals don't feed on humanity, they are simply so large that in their true form they stomp on everything. The ancient Primals agreed to pact because they didn't hold malice for the world. Wardens are all about power. If a warden lets loose, most anything in the world of darkness will be destroyed, along with large sections of the surrounding area. A Beast feeds on the fear of mortals to teach them wisdom, and is connected deeply to a realm of ancient dreams. Primals are elemental titans, drawing power from the elemental connections between their native realm and the elements of this world, and holding their power back to keep from destroying everything. a beast strikes by channeling the strength of the giant through his body, or weaponizing fear. A Warden attacks by creating a talon from nearby stones, or the head of a monster reaches out from a nearby fire to bite their enemy. A beast is a child of the dark mother, and all that crawls through the shadows of the world of darkness is their kin. A Primal is a force of incomparable destruction, experiencing the world through the warden because their true form makes Godzilla look cautious. This is about power constrained, not lessons through fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew thought process.<br /> &quot;I have this great idea for a power/splat/merit/etc/&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no idea if this is balanced, useless, or gamebreaking.&quot;<br /> &quot;I'll ask the internet&quot;<br /> &quot;The thread has died.&quot; <img src=\"images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4226-spiderlord","name":"Spiderlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:19:44-07:00","id":968670,"title":"","content":"After thinking about a bit more, I have come up with a slightly more cogent point. The Primals are destruction incarnate. They come from a realm of endless elemental chaos. If you see a mountain in our world, it is thousands if not millions of years old and will probably last just as long unless we blow it up. If you see a mountain in the primal chaos, it just formed from random rocks smashing together a few moments ago and will be torn about just as quickly. When the primals came to earth in ancient days, it was because they had looked through the boundaries between worlds and seen earth and thought it looked nice. they tried to greet the puny people of this world, which could be compared to a tsunami or wildfire trying to shake hands. The only result is massive destruction and death. the Klisoma (working title) are innate abilities of the primal, to be a force of complete destruction who is themselves indestructible. They cannot add dice to their friends rolls, they cannot heal them. A warden has an easier time tearing down a skyscraper than building a three foot stone wall, and that is supposed to say something. The warden is a channel, a method for the primal to see and hear and touch the world without destroying it. In exchange, the warden is granted some of the primal's near unlimited power, to keep her alive and slay her enemies. if the warden wants to use that power to build, or aid others, or create anything, she must put time and effort into mastering a Klisonoma (also working title) which is more expensive, both in experience and dynam, because you are forcing this near unlimited power into shapes it was never meant to take. And everytime the warden uses that power, some of it bleeds off, resulting in (relatively) minor damage. channel air dynam and electricity will spark or light winds will whip around the area. Earth dynam will crack the suppot beams of buildings or cause the ground you are standing on to shift unpredictably. Water dynam will cause all the damage of years spent in the cold damp in a matter of moments, or freeze the water in nearby pipes; and fire Dynam shouldn't need explaining. and that is only a fraction of the raw destructive power that the primal holds. every moment of a warden's life once they forge the pact is filled with the knowledge that they could tear down everything in their path, but they would also tear down down everything near their path or behind their path, or within shouting distance of their path. The life of a warden is about not taking the easy, selfish and destructive route. Every time they take the easy way, they break something. Every time they slip up, people die. A warden is walking around with the power of a sapient hurricane, trying not to let it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew thought process.<br /> &quot;I have this great idea for a power/splat/merit/etc/&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no idea if this is balanced, useless, or gamebreaking.&quot;<br /> &quot;I'll ask the internet&quot;<br /> &quot;The thread has died.&quot; <img src=\"images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4226-spiderlord","name":"Spiderlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}